# Myriad (CR 702.116a): Tabaxi Toucaneers (3/2) attacks Bot2 in a three-player game. For Bot3, the other opponent, Bot1 may create a token copy
# tapped and attacking: it does, so Bot3 takes the copy's power as Bot2 takes the original's, and the token is exiled at end of
# combat. The card's other keywords (Flying) are on it. Black Lotus and the Moxen pay for it with exactly its cost.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Tabaxi Toucaneers
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Tabaxi Toucaneers.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
? Bot1.Mana =
[T4 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Tabaxi Toucaneers > Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Bot3)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
? Combat.Attackers = Tabaxi Toucaneers > Bot2; Tabaxi Toucaneers > Bot3
? Bot1.Battlefield.Tabaxi Toucaneers#2.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Tabaxi Toucaneers#2.Token = true
[T4 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 17
? Bot3.Life = 17
? Delayed.Count = 0

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Tabaxi Toucaneers.Keywords = Flying
Bot1.Battlefield.Tabaxi Toucaneers#2 = (absent)
Exile.Count = 0
